{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"110019","commit":"877b73f433cdd76b55bc4e46fa17bce8c9db9140","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of `assertDoesNotThrow` and its usage in tests is generally good for reducing boilerplate, but it assumes that any exception thrown indicates a failure condition. This might be appropriate in test contexts where exceptions are not expected, but ensure that this assumption holds true across all uses.","nodes":[{"id":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/ESTestCase.java-test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/ESTestCase.java--98761:99322","promptId":"#9JSBG","srcPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/ESTestCase.java","dstPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/ESTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":98761,"endPos":99322,"startLine":2340,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":2353,"endLineOffset":5,"length":562}]}]},{"comment":"The removal of `actionResult()` calls and their replacement with `result()` calls in tests is mostly correct, but the change in exception handling (from `RuntimeException` to `ExecutionException`) should be verified. Ensure that the tests still correctly validate the expected exceptions and behaviors.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java-3891:3995,4004:4132,4448:4532,4546:4654,4933:5008,5021:5119-4132:4200,4214:4306,4585:4654,4667:4759","promptId":"#0P87E","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/action/support/PlainActionFutureTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3891,"endPos":3995,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":112,"length":105},{"pos":4004,"endPos":4132,"startLine":94,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":94,"endLineOffset":136,"length":129},{"po